            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Rewrite the angle as ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "(n-1)\\pi+\\left(\\frac\\pi2-\\theta\\right)",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", then use the complementary-angle and reciprocal identities.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Adding an integer multiple of $\\pi$ to a cosine argument contributes the factor $(-1)^{n-1}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\sec\\left(\\left(n-\\frac12\\right)\\pi-\\theta\\right)&=\\frac{1}{\\cos\\left((n-1)\\pi+\\left(\\frac\\pi2-\\theta\\right)\\right)}\\\\\n\\sec\\left(\\left(n-\\frac12\\right)\\pi-\\theta\\right)&=\\frac{1}{(-1)^{n-1}\\cos\\left(\\frac\\pi2-\\theta\\right)}\\\\\n\\sec\\left(\\left(n-\\frac12\\right)\\pi-\\theta\\right)&=\\frac{(-1)^{n-1}}{\\sin\\theta}\\\\\n\\sec\\left(\\left(n-\\frac12\\right)\\pi-\\theta\\right)&=(-1)^{n-1}\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta.\n\\end{align*}$$\nThe expression is defined when $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$, equivalently $\\theta\\ne k\\pi$ for an integer $k$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
